m.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8008&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">16 or 17 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Fall</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"jewish-studies-ba__box-2-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_elective&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Elective\\&quot; is an elective slot specific to this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a UB Curriculum-wide component - the exact eligible courses depend on this program&#x27;s requirements as listed in the Undergraduate Catalog.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8008&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"jewish-studies-ba__box-2-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Elementary Hebrew&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;The beginning course of Modern Israeli Hebrew. Essentials of grammar, syntax and conversational practice; elementary reading and writing, common expressions used in daily life, along with introductory knowledge about Israeli culture.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">HEB 101LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Elementary Hebrew</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"jewish-studies-ba__box-2-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Medieval Judaism&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Medieval Judaism is an exploration of Judaism as a minority religion living between the Crescent and Cross, the Islamic and Christian empires between the 9th to 16th centuries. We will explore the dual nature of the medieval period for Jews: part intellectual and cultural flourishing and part persecution and tragedy. Topics to be discussed include: the origins of anti-Semitism, the crusades, philosophy vs. mysticism, the Maimonidean controversy, Jewish-Christian dialogue and polemics, the inquisitions, marranos, responses to tragedy and the Renaissance. This course is the same as HIS 329 and RSP 329, and course repeat rules will apply. Students should consult with their major department regarding any restrictions on their degree requirements.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">JDS 329LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Medieval Judaism</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"jewish-studies-ba__box-2-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Communication Literacy 1: a UB Curriculum Foundations requirement, typically satisfied by ENG 105 or ELI 105.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/foundations.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Communication Literacy</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">14 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"jewish-studies-ba__box-3-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Diversity in the United States\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8008&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Diversity in the United States</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span><div class=\"box-note\">(Approved Diversity in the United States course if not met through approved major, elective, or UBC course.)</div></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"jewish-studies-ba__box-3-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Elementary Modern Hebrew 2&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Hebrew 102 is the second part of the Elementary Hebrew course at UB. This course aims to further present students with the basis of Modern Israeli Hebrew and to assist them in developing the fundamental linguistic skil